  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Sunday) \nIssued at 755 PM CDT Sun Aug 30 2026\n\nThe long term forecast will offer more of the same. At the surface,\nhigh pressure will dominate, keeping temps in the mid to high 90s\nthrough the weekend. With ridging remaining in place in the mid \nlevels too, our saving grace will be the fact that our dew points \nlook to remain in the high 60s to low 70s. This will limit how high \nour heat indices can reach with uncertainty remaining on if we will \nmeet heat advisory criteria. Inversely, since we will be slightly \ndrier, there is some concern for over preforming on current high \ntemperature forecasts. Some deterministic models flirt with triple \ndigit highs this weekend. While we have low confidence in this \noccurring, it will be a trend we keep an eye on. From Sunday forward \nthe forecast becomes somewhat murky. Models have picked up on a \npassing cold front yet are in disagreement on when and if it comes \nthrough. If the cold front does make it through on Sunday as the NBM \nsuggest, highs will drop back to the low 90s. If the front stalls or \ndampens before it gets here, highs will likely remain in the high 90s\nthrough the start of the next work week. make sure to continue to \npractice proper heat safety and check back for updates.",
